:ruby
  PageHeader = import("/components/PageHeader.haml")
  DocsPage = import("/components/DocsPage.haml")
  DocsSection = import("/components/DocsSection.haml")

%DocsPage
  %PageHeader{
    kicker: "Plugin Reference",
    title: "CssPlugin",
    summary: "CssPlugin scopes CSS, emits stylesheet assets, records CSS dependencies, and returns class maps to Ruby and Haml."
  }

  %DocsSection{ title: "Scoped Selectors" }
    :markdown
      CSS is transformed through `mayu-css`. Class selectors become scoped class names, and tag selectors are exposed through `__`-prefixed keys.

      ```css
      article {
        display: grid;
      }

      .featured {
        border-color: var(--color-accent);
      }
      ```

      Ruby and Haml imports receive a class-name map:

      ```ruby
      Styles = import("./Card.css")
      Styles[:featured]
      Styles[:__article]
      ```

  %DocsSection{ title: "CSS Imports" }
    :markdown
      CSS imported from Ruby or Haml returns a class map. CSS imported from CSS records stylesheet dependencies and returns transformed asset paths.

      The same stylesheet should appear once in a rendered document. The example app uses route-scoped asset traversal so root and layout CSS appear before page and component CSS.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Assets" }
    :markdown
      `url(...)` references are resolved through the graph and emitted as assets. External CSS imports can be owned by other plugins, such as `GoogleFontsPlugin`.
